WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.110
A small stone tablet.

2
00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:04.310
No name carved on it yet.

3
00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:08.050
Seven candles in a row, one for each year.

4
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.220
The last flame goes out.

5
00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:14.380
A father writes: "Farewell,
thou child of my right hand,

6
00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:18.980
and joy," Then he calls
his hope for his son a sin.

7
00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:21.670
Why would a grieving father blame himself,

8
00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:23.240
just for loving?

9
00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:27.840
In this mission, you'll meet Ben Jonson,
whose son Benjamin died of the plague

10
00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:30.800
in 1603, aged seven.

11
00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:35.650
You'll puzzle over why a grieving father
talks about his son in money words.

12
00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:40.150
And you'll see how the poem works
like words carved on a gravestone.

13
00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:44.140
Your mission: explain why he
blames himself for loving.
